#################################################################
#  §9  COVERAGE GAP — what this file deliberately does not cover
#################################################################

cvg:3fGhJ5kQwE8rTyU2mNbVcX1
    a mrs:CoverageGap ;
    mrs:gapScope mrs:gs_person_class ;
    mrs:gapDescription "The Companions are estimated at well over 100,000 (Abu Zur'ah al-Razi, via al-Suyuti). This file represents ~35 of them: a curated, historically prominent, documentable set, chosen to demonstrate the network's true shape rather than to claim any completeness. The Badr and Uhud participant lists are similarly highlight sets, not rosters — real Badr had ~313 Muslims present, and Uhud a comparable order of magnitude. Second-generation (Tabi'un) individuals are entirely out of scope for this file by design, per project direction — see docs/09 roadmap. The events between Uhud (3 AH) and the Prophet's death (11 AH) are represented by five milestones (Uhud, Khandaq, Hudaybiyya, the Conquest of Makkah, the Prophet's death) chosen for documentability, not as a complete chronicle — many attested events in this span (Khaybar, the expedition to Tabuk, the Farewell Pilgrimage, among others) are not yet modelled."@en ;
    mrs:gapCause mrs:gc_not_yet_ingested ;
    mrs:knownSource "Sanadset-class narrator datasets; Ibn Hajar's al-Isaba fi tamyiz al-sahaba (the classical biographical dictionary of Companions); Ibn Sa'd's Tabaqat al-Kubra; full participant lists in Ibn Hisham's Sira and Ibn Sa'd; a fuller event chronicle across 3–11 AH."@en .
